# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# The Vitest suite, by project decision. Every test lives in /tests, flattened,
# with the filename recording its subject: lib.csv.rows.test.ts covers
# src/lib/csv/rows.ts.
#
# Consequence, stated so nobody rediscovers it the hard way: the tests are NOT
# in version control, so CI cannot run them and a fresh clone has none. The
# `pnpm test` step was removed from .github/workflows/ci.yml for that reason, and
# vitest.config.mts sets `passWithNoTests` so `pnpm verify` still succeeds for
# someone who has not written them locally. Running the suite is a local
# discipline; the automated nets that remain are the RLS audit, the typecheck,
# the lint and the manual release checklist.
/tests

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the template must be committed, or nobody knows which vars exist.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# netlify
.netlify

# supabase local stack
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp
supabase/.env

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
